  "description": "2D primitive — a FILLED pie wedge: centre (X, Y), Radius, from Start to End angle (degrees). Equal angles = a full disc. Emits a Space polygon.",
  "instructions": "A filled SECTOR (pie wedge) — centre (centerX, centerY), `radius` metres, swept from `startAngle` to `endAngle` (degrees; the sweep is end − start normalised into (0°, 360°], so equal angles give a FULL disc). Unlike Arc (an open stroke) this is a closed, filled Space — door-swing fills, circular stair treads, fan zones. All params wireable. Publishes `val-radius` / `val-sweep`.",
